# Virtual environments
env/
venv/
ENV/
.venv/
# Not just the directory: a worktree commonly gets a `.venv` SYMLINK pointing at
# the main checkout's environment, and `.venv/` (trailing slash) matches only
# directories — so the symlink slips past `git add -A` and gets committed. CI
# then checks it out and `uv sync` dies with "failed to create directory
# `.venv`: File exists". Measured on PR #133.
.venv
env.bak/
venv.bak/

